## 4. Domain Operational Artifacts

### 4.1 Runbooks & Playbooks

| Artifact | Purpose | Source |
|---|---|---|
| **[Template] ML Runbook – Model XXX** | Standard structure: overview, ownership, dashboards, common-issues table, data dependencies, comm channels | W0 §3.4 |
| **[Template] ML Launch Review Checklist** | Pre-experiment + pre-production gates (privacy review, rollback plan, drift monitor, alerting) | W0 §3.5 |
| **Runbook: Managing service nodes for responsible-ai-api** | Concrete reference for service-level ML operations (OTel sidecar race, tenant burst, gevent saturation, ALB decoupling) | W0 §5.2 |
| **ML-Engine Circuit Breaker Runbook** | 20% failure / 60-second sliding-window threshold | W1 §3.2, §4.4 |
| **Auto-generated incident PIRs** | AI MLE drafts PIRs from reasoning traces within 5 business days | W1 §6.3 |

### 4.2 Evaluation & Quality Frameworks

- **rovo-eval** — ConvoAI integration, multi-turn agent simulation, web UI; for end-to-end quality and agent tests [W0 §3.2].
- **AIX-eval** — Pythonic, ML Studio-native, production-data access; for prompt optimization and custom metrics [W0 §3.2].
- **ML Lens** — Production observability, drift detection, alerting [W0 §3.2; W1 §1.1].
- **Evaluation protocol (6 stages):** offline → adhoc → released → packaging → post-packaging verification → shadow/A/B → continuous monitoring [W0 §3.2].
- **Elevated AI-native standards layered on top of the framework** (non-negotiable):
  - Analyze **every** failure case in the eval set; categorize into a taxonomy (data quality, model limitation, feature gap, label noise, distribution shift) [W2 §2.4].
  - Always report **mean ± std across multiple seeds**; never single-seed metrics [W2 §4.2].
  - Always slice by every meaningful dimension (connector type, region, segment, time) before declaring success [W2 §2.4, §4.3].
  - Run full k-fold (or stratified/time-series/group-aware) — never abbreviated for speed [W2 §4.2].
  - Always include both **discrimination metrics and calibration**, plus confidence intervals and fairness checks [W2 §4.3].

### 4.3 Primary Query & Data Patterns

- **MLflow run construction** — standardized run name pattern (`Model_<TS>`), flattened param logging, per-segment metric logging, `mlflow.<framework>.log_model` for artifacts [W0 §3.1].
- **Feature Store lifecycle** — generated → written to Tecton/MLFS → hydrated at inference → logged with request IDs → joined with labels to build training datasets [W0 §3.6].
- **ML Lens queries** — drift metrics (KS test, KL divergence, cosine similarity ≥ 0.60 for NLP embeddings), data-quality dashboards, model-performance dashboards, system-health dashboards [W1 §4.1].
- **TEAMServe/Triton endpoint pattern** — `grpc-teamserve-{region}.{env}.services.kitt-inf.net:443` [W0 §5.2].
- **Cost/utilization queries** — FinOps dashboards, ML Artifact Cost Monitoring [W1 §1.1].

### 4.4 Templates & Standards (regularly produced by the role)

- **Model Card / One-pager** — overview, design decisions, performance, deployment, monitoring [W0 §3.3].
- **Experiment Report** — hypothesis, methodology, controls, expected vs. actual, interpretation, next action, **negative results documented with equal rigor** [W2 §2.2].
- **Deployment Manifest** — intent + non-goals, impacted services/files, declared invariants, risk classification, test plan, rollback plan, post-deploy monitoring plan [W0 §7.4; W1 §3.3].
- **Architecture Comparison Report** — produced before committing to an approach; covers all parallel-explored variants with statistical significance [W2 §3.2].
- **Weekly Experiment Digest** — automated for stakeholders [W1 §6.5].

### 4.5 Reference Materials (canonical)

Internal: AI Employee Strategy, Atlassian Symphony, Policy for AI Agents in SDLC, RFC-002 (AI SDLC Governance, L1–L5), AIF (PAI) L3-O1-KR1, Digital MLE: AI Employee Vision, End-to-End ML Framework @ Atlassian, MLOps@CoreML Long-Term Plan, CoreML Team ML Pipelines Quality Management, Hidden Technical Debt for ML Systems, ML Orchestration Roadmap, Optimus Prime hyperparameter optimization, MLE Agent Capability Evaluation (2026-05-06). Industry: Google Model Cards, MLOps maturity levels, Feast/Tecton design patterns, NVIDIA Triton docs, MLflow conventions [W0 §9; W1 §Sources; W2 §Sources].

