## 9. Challenges & Mitigation Strategies

| Challenge | Type | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|
| **Data / model drift** | Technical | ML Lens automated detection (KS, KL, cosine); drift-triggered retraining (SOP-1); shadow deploys [W1 §4.1] |
| **Feature pipeline failures** (e.g., Tecton outage, UCT minting) | Technical | Fail-open patterns, fallback paths, schema validation, sustained-error alerting [W1 §4.2] |
| **Training instability / job failures** | Technical | Validation + error handling, retry with backoff, ML Studio workflow-limit monitoring, runbook per failure class [W1 §4.3] |
| **Serving latency spikes** (cold starts, Vegas saturation, sidecar coupling) | Technical | Circuit breaker (20% / 60 s), preemptive autoscaling, decoupled health checks, per-tenant limits, canary auto-rollback [W1 §4.4] |
| **Deployment regression despite passing offline eval** | Technical | Shadow + canary + A/B with significance gates; 50/50 rollout pattern; auto-rollback in ~25–45 min cutover window [W1 §4.5] |
| **Reproducibility failures** | Technical | Tarot v3 versioning + complete lineage; MLflow metadata; data versioning; containerized envs; Launchpad pre-prod validation [W1 §4.6] |
| **Adversarial / out-of-distribution inputs** | Technical | Distance-from-training guardrails, safetensors over pickle, red-team testing, continuous distributional anomaly monitoring [W1 §4.7] |
| **Logic drift / unexpected agent behavior** | Organizational (AI-specific) | Agent Reliability Engineer role; calibrated uncertainty enforcement; explicit "I don't know" signals [W1 §5.3; W2 §6.2] |
| **Trust calibration / autonomy expansion gating** | Organizational | Time-to-Delegation metric; data must show safer/faster/more-reliable outcomes vs. manual before tier expansion [W0 §7.6; W1 §8.2] |
| **Cost attribution for 24/7 operation** | Organizational | Per-experiment compute budgets enforced; anomaly detection on cost-vs-historical-median; auto scale-down on convergence [W2 §6.4] |
| **Inter-agent coordination** (shared features across models) | Organizational | Symphony peer-collaboration mode; ORBIT shared context layer (still maturing) [W1 §9.2] |
| **Liability boundaries for autonomous decisions** | Organizational | "Organization, not agent, is accountable"; durable audit trails of intent + evidence + approval basis + outcome [W0 §7.5; W1 §7] |
| **Cross-organization policy composition** | Organizational | Version-controlled, human-authored policies; agent proposes updates, humans approve [W1 §3.1] |

